  "result": "Per-subcommand defaults in `default_map` now reach the subcommand. Your example prints `changed` instead of `normal`, and all 145 tests in `tests/test_commands.py` and `tests/test_defaults.py` pass.\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`), a child context copied the parent's whole `default_map`. It never took the section for its own command name, so `{'foo': {'name': 'changed'}}` was looked up for `name` and missed.\n\n**Fix:** the child now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. If the parent has no section for that command, the child's `default_map` is `None`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_group_subcommand_default_map` to `tests/test_commands.py`. It uses the group, `foo` and `--name` setup from your report and asserts the output is `changed`. I didn't run it against the old code to confirm it failed before the fix.",
